---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { LEGAL, SITE_NAME } from '../site';
const L = LEGAL;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE_NAME} handles your data. Your files are processed in your browser and never uploaded. Learn what analytics and advertising data is collected and your privacy rights.`}
  summary="The short version: the files you open in IconPDF are processed on your own device and are never uploaded to us or anyone else. Like most free websites, we use analytics and advertising services, and this policy explains exactly what they collect and how to opt out."
>
  <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} (iconpdf.com, the "Service") is operated by {L.entity}, {L.entityType} ("we", "us",
    "our"). We are the controller of the limited personal data described in this policy. You can
    contact us at <a href={`mailto:${L.email}`}>{L.email}</a> or by post at the address in
    <a href="#contact">section 13</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="files">2. Your files never leave your device</h2>
  <p>
    Every PDF and image tool on {SITE_NAME} runs locally in your web browser using JavaScript and
    WebAssembly. When you open, edit, convert, compress, sign or otherwise process a file:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>the file is read and processed only in your browser's memory on your own device;</li>
    <li>the file, its contents, its file name and its metadata are <strong>not uploaded</strong> to our servers or to any third party;</li>
    <li>we have no technical ability to see, store, copy or recover your files or the results you download; and</li>
    <li>signatures you draw or type, and watermark or page-number text you enter, stay on your device in the same way.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When you move a file from one tool to another (for example "Chain to another tool"), the file is
    passed between pages through your browser's own local storage (IndexedDB) on your device and
    is deleted once the next tool has loaded it. It is never sent over the network.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because processing is local, we cannot help recover a file if your browser closes or your device
    fails. Always keep your own copy of important documents.
  </p>

  <h2 id="collect">3. Information we do collect</h2>
  <p>We do not ask you to create an account and we do not collect your name, address or payment details to use the Service. We and our service providers collect only the following:</p>
  <h3>a. Usage and device information (analytics)</h3>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics, loaded through Google Tag Manager, to understand how the Service is used
    so we can improve it. It collects information such as pages visited, time on page, the tools you
    open, referring website, approximate location (city or country, derived from your IP address),
    browser type, device type, operating system, screen size and language. It uses cookies and
    similar identifiers to recognise repeat visits. It does not receive your files or their contents.
  </p>
  <h3>b. Advertising information</h3>
  <p>
    The Service is free because it shows advertising served by Google AdSense. Google and its partners
    may use cookies, device identifiers and your IP address to serve ads, limit how often you see an
    ad, measure ad performance, prevent fraud and, where permitted and you have not opted out, show
    ads based on your interests and your visits to this and other websites. See
    <a href="#ads">section 6</a> for how to control this.
  </p>
  <h3>c. Technical and security logs</h3>
  <p>
    Our hosting and content-delivery provider, Cloudflare, processes the technical information any
    web server needs to deliver a page, such as your IP address, the page requested, the time of the
    request and your browser's user agent, and may retain it for a limited period for security,
    abuse prevention and reliability.
  </p>
  <h3>d. Information you send us</h3>
  <p>
    If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you choose to include in your
    message. We use it only to respond and keep a record of the correspondence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use">4. How we use information and our legal bases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>To provide and secure the Service</strong> (delivering pages, preventing abuse): our legitimate interests in operating a safe, reliable website.</li>
    <li><strong>To measure and improve the Service</strong> (analytics): your consent where the law requires it, otherwise our legitimate interests.</li>
    <li><strong>To fund the Service with advertising</strong>: your consent where the law requires it (for example in the EEA, UK and Switzerland), otherwise our legitimate interests.</li>
    <li><strong>To respond to you</strong>: to answer your request, and our legitimate interests in keeping records.</li>
    <li><strong>To comply with law</strong>: to meet legal obligations, enforce our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and protect our rights.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use your information to make decisions that produce legal or similarly significant effects about you.</p>

  <h2 id="sharing">5. Who we share information with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your files, and we never have them to share. We share the limited information described above only with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google LLC</strong>, for analytics (Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager), advertising (Google AdSense) and web fonts (Google Fonts, which receives your IP address when your browser downloads the fonts). See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong>, for hosting, content delivery and security.</li>
    <li><strong>Hugging Face, Inc.</strong>, only if you use the Remove Background tool: your browser downloads the AI model files from Hugging Face's servers, which see your IP address as with any download. Your image is not sent to them.</li>
    <li><strong>Authorities or other parties</strong> when required by law, to respond to legal process, to protect the rights, property or safety of us, our users or others, or in connection with a merger, acquisition or sale of assets, in which case this policy will continue to apply to the information transferred.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="ads">6. Cookies, advertising and your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a> lists the cookies and browser storage we and our partners
    use. You can control them in several ways:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consent tools:</strong> visitors in the EEA, UK and Switzerland are asked for consent before non-essential cookies are used for advertising and analytics, and can change their choice at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Personalised ads:</strong> turn off personalised advertising from Google at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Ad Settings</a>, or opt out of many third-party advertising networks at <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info" rel="noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a> (US) or <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu" rel="noopener" target="_blank">youronlinechoices.eu</a> (EU).</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Browser controls:</strong> block or delete cookies in your browser settings. The tools keep working if you do.</li>
    <li><strong>Global Privacy Control:</strong> where required by law, we treat a GPC signal from your browser as a request to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information for targeted advertising.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="retention">7. How long we keep information</h2>
  <p>
    We keep no copies of your files because we never receive them. Google Analytics data is kept for
    the retention period configured in our account (no longer than 14 months for user-level data).
    Advertising and hosting providers keep data according to their own policies. We keep emails you
    send us for as long as needed to deal with your request and for our records, and then delete them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">8. Your privacy rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or receive a copy
    of personal information we hold about you; to object to or restrict certain processing; to
    withdraw consent at any time (without affecting earlier processing); and to complain to a data
    protection authority. Because we do not run accounts and do not receive your files, we usually
    hold very little that can be linked to you, but we will honour every request we can.
  </p>
  <p>
    To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${L.email}`}>{L.email}</a> with "Privacy request" in
    the subject. We may need to verify your request, and we will respond within the time required by
    applicable law (generally within 30 days, or 45 days under US state laws). You may use an
    authorised agent where the law allows. We will not discriminate against you for exercising your
    rights.
  </p>

  <h2 id="us-states">9. Notice for California and other US state residents</h2>
  <p>
    In the last 12 months we have collected the following categories of personal information:
    identifiers (such as IP address and cookie or device identifiers), internet or other electronic
    network activity information (such as pages viewed and interactions with ads), and approximate
    geolocation. We collect them from you and your device for the purposes described in
    <a href="#use">section 4</a>, and disclose them to the service providers and advertising partners
    listed in <a href="#sharing">section 5</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information for money. However, allowing advertising partners to use
    cookies for interest-based advertising may be considered "selling" or "sharing" personal
    information under California, Colorado, Connecticut, Virginia and similar state laws. You can opt
    out at any time by using the controls in <a href="#ads">section 6</a>, by enabling Global Privacy
    Control, or by emailing us with "Do not sell or share my personal information" in the subject.
    We do not knowingly sell or share the personal information of consumers under 16. We do not
    collect sensitive personal information.
  </p>

  <h2 id="international">10. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    {L.entity} is based in the United States, and our service providers may process information in
    the United States and other countries. Where we or our providers transfer personal information
    from the EEA, UK or Switzerland, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as the European
    Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses or the EU-US Data Privacy Framework where the
    recipient is certified.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">11. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The Service is not directed to children under 13 (or under 16 in the EEA and UK), and we do not
    knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child has provided us with
    personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top shows when it
    last changed. If we make material changes, such as starting to upload or store user files, we
    will give clear notice on the Service before the change takes effect.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">13. Contact us</h2>
  <address>
    {L.entity}<br />
    {L.address.map((line) => (<>{line}<br /></>))}
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${L.email}`}>{L.email}</a>
  </address>
</LegalPage>
